+# Key Rotation Playbook (HSM / KMS)
+
+Overview
+- Key rotation for cosign keys backing critical delegated manifests should be executed carefully with no loss of verification capability.
+
+Steps (operator)
+1. Prepare new keys in each cloud KMS / HSM that participates in threshold signing.
+2. Add new key refs to VAULT at path secret/data/aegis/kms/<provider> (use ops/vault/sync_kms_per_cloud.sh).
+3. Update COSIGN_KEY_REFS (comma-separated) in Vault or deployment config in a staging environment.
+4. Run a re-sign job:
+   - Enumerate active high-value artifacts (delegation manifests, attestation bundles).
+   - Re-sign with new keys using ops/hsm/multi_sign_orchestrator.py.
+   - Upload new signatures and record metadata in Vault.
+5. Verify:
+   - cosign verify for both old and new keys (public-key verification) succeeds for a sample set.
+6. Roll forward to production only after verification.
+7. Retire old keys per org policy after ensuring evidence still verifies with archived public keys.
+
+Emergency rollback
+- If rotation causes verification failures, revert COSIGN_KEY_REFS to previous value and re-deploy validators/webhooks.
+
